Z||000000||RZURCTN||12-01-1999||11:47 PM||||I didn't even know that I had it until tonight.  How does it attach and where?  While my 84SE has the sunroof, it doesn't have the sunshade.  I found the deflector under the "hood", but I don't know how to hook it up.  If anyone knows could you please give me some instructions?  Thanks a lot!!!||||reg||5
Z||000001||88GT||12-02-1999||01:53 AM||||I"m not sure if it is the same as on the 87GT that I used to have.  If it is here it goes.<P>There should be two metal clips.  One on either end.  They will slide down into corresponing slots on the frame of the sunroof.  Just slide these clips in and you should be all set to go.<P>James||||reg||1
Z||000002||RossT||12-02-1999||02:03 AM||||If you have your owners manual, there should<BR>be a detailed diagram, at leat my 88 owners<BR>manual has it.<P>Ross||||reg||1
Z||000003||Carrolles||12-02-1999||06:54 AM||||This may seem obvious to everyone but I'll say it anyway for the uninformed.<P>The deflector is used only when the sunroof panel is out of the car and attaches where the sunroof panel attaches.<P>When not in use the sunroof panel stores under the front storage compartment on the rubber supports.||||reg||1
Z||000004||TOM||12-02-1999||11:44 AM||||Your 84 shouldn't have a sunshade. I dont know when they came out with it but I think it was somewhere in the middle of production.||||reg||1
